<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs-Thursday est 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs-Thursday est 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and gilts 1.00 lower than mid-session Wednesday. Trade slow to moderate for light demand and offerings.</p>
<p>Thursdays  estimate: 100000  Wk ago: 107000  Yr ago: 110000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>			   Country		  Plants</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    52.50 -53.50	   53.50 -54.50</p>
<p>few			52.00 -54.00	   53.00  55.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    50.50 -53.50	   51.00 -54.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    47.00 -52.00	   47.50 -53.00</p>
<p>Sows:  steady.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  43.00 -44.00	   43.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   43.00 -48.00	   45.00 -48.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    47.00 -51.00	   47.00 -52.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean.</p>
<p>Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
